    <briefdescription>
<para>: a class that contains pointers to topologically (and most often also physically) collocated nodes. SplitBoundaries (node-matching standalone mesh patches connected by interface elements typically consist of <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_node_manifold" kindref="compound">NodeManifold</ref> objects. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="attention"><para>the nodes on the perimeter of a <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_split_boundary" kindref="compound">SplitBoundary</ref> that terminates in a volume are not duplicated! - therefore they are not manifolds. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
